<title>USA: COMEX copper called to open unchanged.</title>
<headline>COMEX copper called to open unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>COMEX copper futures were called to open unchanged Tuesday despite some modest gains on LME overnight which were soon pared.</p>
<p>LME reported Tuesday that stocks fell 2,125 tonnes to 155,775 tonnes.</p>
<p>COMEX stocks rose 1,373 short tons Monday to 43,935 short tons.</p>
<p>COMEX May copper closed at 105.45 cents a lb Monday, and traded 105.95 to 105.45 cents on ACCESS.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
